   "date": "2017-11-16T01:14:16Z",
   "subject": "Goodness of fit when one parameter is fixed",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi everyone, <div><br></div><div>Hopefully this isn&#39;t a redundant topic but I haven&#39;t been able to find a previous thread that addresses it. I am using dynamic n-mixture models to estimate tadpole density and survival over the course of the summer. Because there shouldn&#39;t be any recruitment over my trapping period, I fixed the gamma parameter:</div><div><br></div><div><div>am5 &lt;- pcountOpen(~WetlandType+ElevationM+Year, ~1, ~1, ~offset(log(numTraps)) , AmtiAbundUmf, K=50,fix= &quot;gamma&quot;, mixture=&quot;ZIP&quot;)</div></div><div><br></div><div>When I try to evaluate goodness of fit using the Nmix.gof.test or parboot functions I get the error:</div><div><div><br></div><div>Nmix.gof.test(am5, nsim = 50)</div></div><div>&quot;Error in Xgam %*% coef(object, &quot;gamma&quot;) : requires numeric/complex matrix/vector arguments&quot;<br></div><div><br></div><div>Does anyone know of a way to get around this problem? These functions work just fine when I allow gamma to be estimated. </div><div><br></div><div>If not, any thoughts on whether I can evaluate goodness of fit with gamma in the model?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you!</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "GbEgJwTdAgAJ",
   "from": "Richard Chandler",
   "author": "403be63af7ebf220",
   "date": "2017-11-16T14:41:35Z",
   "subject": "Re: [unmarked] Goodness of fit when one parameter is fixed",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Hi Leah,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">This looks like a bug:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">&gt; (m1 &lt;- pcountOpen(~1, ~1, ~1, ~1, umf, K=20, fix=&quot;gamma&quot;))\r\n\r\nCall:\r\npcountOpen(lambdaformula = ~1, gammaformula = ~1, omegaformula = ~1, \r\n    pformula = ~1, data = umf, K = 20, fix = &quot;gamma&quot;)\r\n\r\nAbundance:\r\n Estimate    SE    z  P(&gt;|z|)\r\n     2.36 0.112 21.1 4.39e-99\r\n\r\nApparent Survival:\r\n Estimate   SE     z P(&gt;|z|)\r\n     12.2 24.4 0.498   0.618\r\n\r\nDetection:\r\n Estimate    SE    z  P(&gt;|z|)\r\n   -0.727 0.158 -4.6 4.26e-06\r\n\r\nAIC: 996.7418 \r\n&gt; simulate(m1)\r\nError in Xgam %*% coef(object, &quot;gamma&quot;) : \r\n  requires numeric/complex matrix/vector arguments\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">I just added it to the to-do list: <a href=\"https://github.com/rbchan/unmarked/issues/110\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rbchan/unmarked/issues/110&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451685302000&amp;usg=AOvVaw02cPSmXOnPblIbDLtkf7Bx\">https://github.com/rbchan/unmarked/issues/110</a></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Thanks,<br>Richard</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdiBjbGFzcz0iZ21haWwtbWFya2Rvd24taGVyZS13cmFwcGVyIj48cCBzdHlsZT0ibWFyZ2lu\r\nOiAwcHggMHB4IDEuMmVtOyI+SGkgTGVhaCw8YnI+PC9wPjwvZGl2PjxkaXYgY2xhc3M9ImdtYWls\r\nX2Rl