ses it. I am using dynamic n-mixture models to estimate tadpole density and survival over the course of the summer. Because there shouldn&#39;t be any recruitment over my trapping period, I fixed the gamma parameter:</div><div><br></div><div><div>am5 &lt;- pcountOpen(~WetlandType+ElevationM+Year, ~1, ~1, ~offset(log(numTraps)) , AmtiAbundUmf, K=50,fix= &quot;gamma&quot;, mixture=&quot;ZIP&quot;)</div></div><div><br></div><div>When I try to evaluate goodness of fit using the Nmix.gof.test or parboot functions I get the error:</div><div><div><br></div><div>Nmix.gof.test(am5, nsim = 50)</div></div><div>&quot;Error in Xgam %*% coef(object, &quot;gamma&quot;) : requires numeric/complex matrix/vector arguments&quot;<br></div><div><br></div><div>Does anyone know of a way to get around this problem? These functions work just fine when I allow gamma to be estimated. </div><div><br></div><div>If not, any thoughts on whether I can evaluate goodness of fit with gamma in the model?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you!</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div></font></span></div></span><span><font color=\"#888888\"><span>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;unmarked&quot; group.<br></span>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">unmarked+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<span><br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451685306000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3K6uOx_fEQ3Luzw7zZEGnl\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</span></font></span></blockquote></div><span><br><br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div>-- <br><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Richard Chandler<div>Assistant 